 Every key on the calculator keypad is reachable with the pointer.

 The pane hit-tests by laying its tree out again rather than by memoizing
 the drawn one, and that is safe here for a reason the browser could not
 use: the calculator's state is a `poke-32` block, not heap, so nothing is
 allocated above the tree that a release would take with it. The bounds are
 the same either way, because `comp-render` lays out exactly the tree the
 paint hands it and nothing else.

 The scan hoists the layout OUT of the probe deliberately. `dk-calc-hit`
 lays the tree out on every call, which is right for a click that happens
 when a person moves their hand and wrong for a test that probes thousands
 of points: at one layout per point this would run for minutes and measure
 the layout rather than the mapping. The two spot checks below still go
 through `dk-calc-hit` itself, so the bundled function is not left untested.

 THE REFERENCE LAYOUT MOVED WITH THE PANE, and the arm was REPAIRED rather
 than re-baselined (L-INSTRUMENT). The Calculator is a window now, so its tree
 is laid out inside the window's content box through `comp-render-at` and no
 longer at the screen corner under the full-width chrome. A hoisted layout
 built the old way would still produce a tidy table of reachable scancodes,
 and every one of them would name the key at that offset from the CORNER
 rather than the key under the pointer -- a click landing on a
 wrong-but-plausible digit, which is the failure a screenshot cannot show.
 So the hoisted layout repeats `dk-calc-hit`'s own rect arithmetic, and the
 two spot checks are what tie the copy back to the original.

 `ds` CELL 24 IS NOW LOAD-BEARING HERE and it was never set. `dk-calc-hit`
 reads the calculator's block out of that cell to find the window rect, and an
 unwritten cell reads zero, so the rect came off ADDRESS ZERO -- the exact
 "a cell nobody writes reads as zero, and zero is a writable address" trap
 `works-desk-contract.md` section 2 records against the Edit pane.

 AND NO ROW ABOVE CAN TELL, which is why the placed row below exists. Measured
 2026-08-25 by deleting the `poke-32`: every row still passed. Address zero
 reads as zeros, zeros mean `dk-wnd-st-normal` and a width of zero means
 never-placed, so the wrong block yields exactly the default rect the right
 block yields, and the two agree for as long as no window is ever moved. A
 guard whose sabotage moves nothing is not a guard, so the last row PLACES a
 window on its own block and asks the same question there: the default rect
 and a placed rect disagree, so that row reads the cell for real.

 The expected scancodes are the ones `gcalc-key` already dispatches:
 2 to 11 are digits 1-9 then 0, 12 is minus, 13 is plus, 28 is equals, 53 is
 divide, 55 is multiply. Fifteen buttons, and the keypad draws no C, so 46
 (clear) is keyboard-only and its absence here is correct rather than a gap.

Section: Test

  hit-at : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  hit-at (laid) (x) (y) =
    when ev-hit-widget laid x y
      is Just (wgt) -> gcalc-id-scan (wgt.wn-id)
      is None -> 0

  scan-row : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scan-row (laid) (seen) (x) (y) =
    if x >= 1024 then 0
    else let sc = hit-at laid x y
    in let p = if sc /= 0 then poke-byte seen sc 1 else 0
    in scan-row laid seen (x + 8) y

  scan-grid : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scan-grid (laid) (seen) (y) =
    if y >= 768 then 0
    else let r = scan-row laid seen 0 y
    in scan-grid laid seen (y + 8)

 THE SCALED PATH IS TESTED BY ITS OWN ARITHMETIC, not by a second sweep.
 Above 1600 the tree is laid out in LOGICAL pixels at half the panel and the
 pointer still arrives in DEVICE pixels, so `dk-calc-hit` divides. A wrong
 divide is invisible to the 1024 sweep, which runs at scale 1 where dividing
 by one hides it. This finds the first logical point that hits any key, then
 asks `dk-calc-hit` for the DEVICE point at twice those coordinates: the two
 must answer the same key, and they can only do that if the divide is right.

  yn2 : Boolean -> Text
  yn2 (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  fh-row : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fh-row (laid) (x) (y) =
    if x >= 960 then 0 - 1
    else if hit-at laid x y /= 0 then x
    else fh-row laid (x + 4) y

  fh : WidgetNode, Integer -> Integer
  fh (laid) (y) =
    if y >= 540 then 0 - 1
    else let x = fh-row laid 0 y
    in if x >= 0 then x * 1000 + y else fh laid (y + 4)

  seen-text : Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  seen-text (seen) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 64 then acc
    else if peek-byte seen i == 1 then seen-text seen (i + 1) (acc & " " & integer-to-text i)
    else seen-text seen (i + 1) acc

 The window's content box in LOGICAL units, which is what `comp-render-at`
 lays a window's tree out in and therefore what `dk-calc-hit` divides into.
 The titlebar comes off the top, because the tree starts below it.

  cc-tree : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  cc-tree (ks) (w) (h) (ds) =
    let s = ui-wscale w
    in let st = dk-wnd-st ks
    in let bh = dk-wnd-bar-h gfont-none s
    in let wx = dk-wnd-rx ks w st
    in let wy = dk-wnd-ry ks w h st ds + bh
    in let ww = dk-wnd-rw ks w st
    in let wh = dk-wnd-rh ks w h st ds - bh
    in widget-layout (gcalc-tree ks) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect (wx / s) (wy / s) (ww / s) (wh / s))

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ks = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let seen = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let gp = poke-32 ds desk-gpu-cell 1
    in let kp = poke-32 ds 24 ks
    in let laid = cc-tree ks 1024 768 ds
    in let g = scan-grid laid seen 0
    in let hd-tree = cc-tree ks 1920 1080 ds
    in let hd-p = fh hd-tree 0
    in let hd-x = hd-p / 1000
    in let hd-y = int-mod hd-p 1000
    in let hd-logical = if hd-p < 0 then 0 else hit-at hd-tree hd-x hd-y
    in let hd-device = if hd-p < 0 then 0 else dk-calc-hit 1920 1080 ks (hd-x * 2) (hd-y * 2) ds gfont-none
    in let ks2 = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let ds2 = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap2 = poke-32 ds2 dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let gp2 = poke-32 ds2 desk-gpu-cell 1
    in let kp2 = poke-32 ds2 24 ks2
    in let pl = dk-wnd-place ks2 (dk-wnd-x 1024 dk-wnd-st-normal + 40) (dk-wnd-y 1024 768 dk-wnd-st-normal ds2 + 24) 300 260
    in let pl-tree = cc-tree ks2 1024 768 ds2
    in let pl-p = fh pl-tree 0
    in let pl-x = pl-p / 1000
    in let pl-y = int-mod pl-p 1000
    in let pl-ref = if pl-p < 0 then 0 else hit-at pl-tree pl-x pl-y
    in let pl-hit = if pl-p < 0 then 0 else dk-calc-hit 1024 768 ks2 pl-x pl-y ds2 gfont-none
    in act
      print-line-uni ("reachable" & seen-text seen 0 "")
      print-line-uni ("miss sc=" & integer-to-text (dk-calc-hit 1024 768 ks 0 0 ds gfont-none))
      print-line-uni ("sidebar sc=" & integer-to-text (dk-calc-hit 1024 768 ks 60 300 ds gfont-none))
      print-line-uni ("hd logical == device: " & yn2 (hd-logical /= 0 & hd-logical == hd-device))
      print-line-uni ("placed: reference " & integer-to-text pl-ref & " hit " & integer-to-text pl-hit & " agree " & yn2 (pl-ref /= 0 & pl-ref == pl-hit))
    end
